    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 39 tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection in the owner-create flow into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`**\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a transient `getIdentityKey()` computing the key from the already-normalized stored fields (telephone in E.164, lower-cased email, household id).\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced the three separate checks (telephone, email, household) with:\n   - Household resolution first (unchanged logic \u2014 when `sharesHousehold` is true and a same-lastName/address household exists, assign the shared `householdId` and backfill members), but it **no longer throws** on a household match.\n   - A single identity check that rejects with **409** only when the new owner's whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's.\n   - Removed the now-unused `isEmailInUse` helper and stale imports.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/DuplicateIdentityException.java`** (new) + **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 new exception mapped to 409 Conflict.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` string field to the `Owner` schema so it's returned in responses (the DTO/mapper pick it up automatically).\n\nBehavioral consequence, as specified: because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with **different** telephones now have different identity keys and are both allowed (Cp11, Cp23); only an exact full-key match is a duplicate (Cp03, Cp10, Cp25, Cp28).",
